<section class="get" id="get">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="get-card">
      <span class="eyebrow">Get Ari</span>
      <h2>Not out yet — but close.</h2>
      <p>Ari's in active pre-release, and the Android build is already going out to testers. Put your name down and you'll get it on your phone — or star the repo if you would rather just follow along.</p>
      <div class="cta-row">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/tester">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9.5 3h5M10.5 3v6.2L5.3 18a2 2 0 0 0 1.7 3h10a2 2 0 0 0 1.7-3l-5.2-8.8V3"/><path d="M8 14.5h8"/></svg>
          Become a tester
        </a>
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="https://github.com/ari-digital-assistant">
          <svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M12 .5l3.09 6.26L22 7.77l-5 4.87 1.18 6.88L12 16.27 5.82 19.52 7 12.64 2 7.77l6.91-1.01z"/></svg>
          Star on GitHub
        </a>
        <span class="badge-soon">F-Droid &amp; Google Play — coming soon</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<style>
  /* Ported verbatim from docs/design-reference/dusk-mockup.html's
     <section class="get"> block. Shared .eyebrow/.wrap/.btn/.btn-primary +
     section padding live in global.css. */
  .get{position:relative; overflow:hidden}
  .get-card{
    background:var(--plum-ink); color:#F6EDE1; border-radius:24px; padding:56px 44px; text-align:center;
    position:relative; overflow:hidden; border:1px solid var(--hair);
  }
  .get-card::before{content:""; position:absolute; inset:auto -10% -60% -10%; height:80%;
    background:radial-gradient(ellipse at 50% 100%, var(--glow), transparent 70%);}
  .get-card .eyebrow{color:var(--amber); position:relative}
  .get-card h2{font-size:clamp(28px,4vw,42px); margin-top:14px; position:relative}
  .get-card p{color:#D9C3D0; max-width:46ch; margin:16px auto 0; position:relative}
  .get-card .cta-row{display:flex; gap:14px; justify-content:center; margin-top:30px; position:relative; flex-wrap:wrap}
  /* The shared .btn-ghost is built for the page background, not for this card.
     Its light --surface fill would out-shout the primary button sitting next to
     it, and in dark mode it collapses into the plum instead. So it borrows the
     card's own palette — the same translucent white .badge-soon already uses. */
  .get-card .btn-ghost{background:transparent; border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.22); color:#F6EDE1}
  .get-card .btn-ghost:hover{border-color:rgba(255,255,255,.5)}
  .badge-soon{display:inline-flex; align-items:center; gap:8px; font-family:var(--mono); font-size:12px; color:#D9C3D0; border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.16); border-radius:999px; padding:8px 14px}
</style>
